 <h1>WoW Forever builds</h1><p class="lede">65 talent builds for all nine classes, each with a level-by-level order from 10 to 60 and a calculator link. Meta builds are what most players run; off-meta builds are the uncommon ones that can work.</p>
 <p><a href="#warrior">Warrior</a> · <a href="#paladin">Paladin</a> · <a href="#hunter">Hunter</a> · <a href="#rogue">Rogue</a> · <a href="#priest">Priest</a> · <a href="#shaman">Shaman</a> · <a href="#mage">Mage</a> · <a href="#warlock">Warlock</a> · <a href="#druid">Druid</a></p><h2 id="warrior" style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px"><img src="../img/icons/class-warrior.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" style="border-radius:7px">Warrior</h2><div class="cols2"><div><h3 style="color:#8fc4e8">Meta <span class="pill">5</span></h3><p class="old" style="margin:-4px 0 10px">The builds most players run.</p><div class="stack"><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="warrior-arms-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Arms two-hander</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Two-hander Mortal Strike build with Weaponmaster, Improved Slam and Bloodthrill, dipping Fury for Cruelty, Unbridled Wrath and Booming Voice.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>32 / 17 / 2</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="warrior-fury-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Fury dual-wield</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Dual-wield Bloodthirst build with Flurry, Improved Whirlwind and full Dual Wield Specialization, taking Arms down to Impale and Anger Management.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>17 / 34 / 0</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="warrior-prot-tank.html"><span class="tag ">Tank</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Protection shield tank</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Shield Slam tank with Bastion, Defiance, Focused Rage and Improved Revenge; Arms gives Deflection, Tactical Mastery and Anger Management.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>11 / 5 / 35</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="warrior-arms-leveling.html"><span class="tag lv">Leveling</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Arms leveling</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Rend, Overpower and Deep Wounds early, Sweeping Strikes at 30, Mortal Strike at 40, then Fury for crit and rage.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>31 / 20 / 0</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="warrior-arms-pvp.html"><span class="tag ">PvP</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Arms PvP</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Mortal Strike with Improved Hamstring 3 to stop kiting, plus Fury for Cruelty, Enrage and Piercing Howl.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>31 / 20 / 0</b> · level order →</p></a></div></div><div><h3 style="color:var(--ember)">Off-meta <span class="pill">1</span></h3><p class="old" style="margin:-4px 0 10px">Uncommon builds that can work – try something different.</p><div class="stack"><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="warrior-fury-prot-tank.html"><span class="tag ">Tank</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Bloodthirst tank (Fury/Protection)</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">A shield tank that goes 31 deep into Fury for Bloodthirst, Death Wish and Flurry, keeping only the shield and rage basics from Protection.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>3 / 31 / 17</b> · level order →</p></a></div></div></div><h2 id="paladin" style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px"><img src="../img/icons/class-paladin.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" style="border-radius:7px">Paladin</h2><div class="cols2"><div><h3 style="color:#8fc4e8">Meta <span class="pill">6</span></h3><p class="old" style="margin:-4px 0 10px">The builds most players run.</p><div class="stack"><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="paladin-ret-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Retribution two-hander</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Vengeance, Champion of the Light and Unsealed Wrath with a two-hander, plus Improved Seals and Holy Conduit from Holy and Divine Intellect and Precision for hit.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>12 / 8 / 31</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="paladin-prot-tank.html"><span class="tag ">Tank</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Protection tank (Seal damage)</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Holy Shield, Reckoning, Iron Creed and Shieldsworn by 40, then Divine Strength and Improved Seals from Holy and Deflection from Retribution for damage and parry.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>13 / 31 / 7</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="paladin-deep-prot-tank.html"><span class="tag ">Tank</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Deep Protection tank</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Takes nearly every defensive Protection talent (Toughness 5, Anticipation 5, Divine Intellect 5) and puts the rest into cheaper Judgements.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>0 / 43 / 8</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="paladin-holy-healer.html"><span class="tag ">Healer</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Holy healer</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Illumination, Holy Shock, Boundless Light, Holy Power and Light's Vigil, with Divine Intellect and Redoubt from Protection and Benediction from Retribution.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>32 / 14 / 5</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="paladin-ret-leveling.html"><span class="tag lv">Leveling</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Retribution leveling</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Benediction, Conviction and Seal of Command first, Repentance at 30 and Unsealed Wrath at 40, then Divine Strength, Improved Seals and Divine Intellect.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>15 / 5 / 31</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="paladin-holy-pvp.html"><span class="tag ">PvP</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Holy PvP healer</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">The full healing Holy tree plus Toughness, Redoubt and Divine Intellect for survival; no Retribution.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>32 / 19 / 0</b> · level order →</p></a></div></div><div><h3 style="color:var(--ember)">Off-meta <span class="pill">2</span></h3><p class="old" style="margin:-4px 0 10px">Uncommon builds that can work – try something different.</p><div class="stack"><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="paladin-shockadin.html"><span class="tag ">DPS</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Shockadin (two-hander + Holy Shock)</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">A two-hander Retribution base stopping at Champion of the Light, with Holy down to Holy Shock so you can Shock and Consecrate between swings.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>23 / 0 / 28</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="paladin-shock-tank.html"><span class="tag ">Tank</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Holy Shock tank (Holy/Protection)</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">A shield tank that swaps deep Protection for Holy Shock, Illumination and Improved Seals while keeping Holy Shield, Swift Judgement and Improved Righteous Fury.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>27 / 24 / 0</b> · level order →</p></a></div></div></div><h2 id="hunter" style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px"><img src="../img/icons/class-hunter.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" style="border-radius:7px">Hunter</h2><div class="cols2"><div><h3 style="color:#8fc4e8">Meta <span class="pill">5</span></h3><p class="old" style="margin:-4px 0 10px">The builds most players run.</p><div class="stack"><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="hunter-bm-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Beast Mastery</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Pet-centred damage: Frenzy, Ferocity and Bestial Wrath on the pet, with Marksmanship picked up to Mortal Shots for your own crits and Trueshot Aura.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>31 / 20 / 0</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="hunter-mm-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Marksmanship Lone Wolf</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Petless deep Marksmanship: Lone Wolf for +20% damage, Sniper Shot, Barrage and Ranged Weapon Specialization, with Deadly Aspects for Auto Shot haste.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>5 / 46 / 0</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="hunter-sv-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Survival Lone Wolf</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Lone Wolf Survival that weaves Mongoose Bite, Strider Kick and Lacerating Strikes bleeds between shots, scaling off the 15% Agility from Lightning Reflexes.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>5 / 13 / 33</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="hunter-bm-leveling.html"><span class="tag lv">Leveling</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Beast Mastery leveling</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Let the pet tank and kill: Improved Revive Pet and Pathfinding early, Summon Hawk and Intimidation mid-way, Bestial Wrath at 40, then Marksmanship crit and Trueshot Aura.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>33 / 18 / 0</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="hunter-mm-pvp.html"><span class="tag ">PvP</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Marksmanship PvP</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Ranged burst with Sniper Shot and Mortal Shots plus lots of control: Improved Concussive Shot stuns, Scatter Shot, and Survival's Entrapment, Improved Wing Clip, Deterrence and Counterattack.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>0 / 31 / 20</b> · level order →</p></a></div></div><div><h3 style="color:var(--ember)">Off-meta <span class="pill">2</span></h3><p class="old" style="margin:-4px 0 10px">Uncommon builds that can work – try something different.</p><div class="stack"><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="hunter-melee-sv.html"><span class="tag ">DPS</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Melee Survival with pet</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Keeps the pet and goes properly melee: Predator's Edge, Expose Prey into Mongoose Bite, Lacerating Strikes bleeds and Strider Kick, with Deflection, Deterrence and Counterattack for survivability.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>7 / 11 / 33</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="hunter-pet-mm.html"><span class="tag ">DPS</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Marksmanship with pet</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Deep Marksmanship to Sniper Shot but keeps a pet out, taking Beast Mastery's Unleashed Fury, Ferocity and Summon Hawk instead of Lone Wolf.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>20 / 31 / 0</b> · level order →</p></a></div></div></div><h2 id="rogue" style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px"><img src="../img/icons/class-rogue.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" style="border-radius:7px">Rogue</h2><div class="cols2"><div><h3 style="color:#8fc4e8">Meta <span class="pill">5</span></h3><p class="old" style="margin:-4px 0 10px">The builds most players run.</p><div class="stack"><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="rogue-mutilate-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Mutilate</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Dual-dagger Mutilate with Venom, Relentless Strikes and Seal Fate, plus Combat for hit, Puncturing Wounds and cheaper Eviscerate.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>31 / 20 / 0</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="rogue-combat-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Combat</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Hack and Slash, Flash of Steel and Adrenaline Rush with Aggression and Weapon Expertise; Assassination for Malice and Lethality.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>12 / 35 / 4</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="rogue-sub-dungeon.html"><span class="tag ">Dungeon</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Subtlety Hemorrhage / Death Mark</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Hemorrhage, Boot Knife, Shank and Death Mark with Ambush openers, plus Malice and Improved Slice and Dice.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>11 / 9 / 31</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="rogue-combat-leveling.html"><span class="tag lv">Leveling</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Combat leveling</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Sinister Strike, Riposte and Blade Flurry by 30 and Adrenaline Rush at 40, with any weapon type, then Malice, Lethality and Cold Blood.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>20 / 31 / 0</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="rogue-sub-pvp.html"><span class="tag ">PvP</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Subtlety PvP</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Setup, Initiative, Dirty Deeds/Tricks and Elusiveness for openers and control, with Combat Lightning Reflexes, Improved Kick and Improved Sprint.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>5 / 17 / 29</b> · level order →</p></a></div></div><div><h3 style="color:var(--ember)">Off-meta <span class="pill">1</span></h3><p class="old" style="margin:-4px 0 10px">Uncommon builds that can work – try something different.</p><div class="stack"><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="rogue-sub-leveling.html"><span class="tag lv">Leveling</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Subtlety Hemorrhage leveling</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Levels as Subtlety instead of the usual Combat: Setup and Opportunity first, Hemorrhage at 30 and Death Mark at 40, then Assassination for crit.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>20 / 0 / 31</b> · level order →</p></a></div></div></div><h2 id="priest" style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px"><img src="../img/icons/class-priest.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" style="border-radius:7px">Priest</h2><div class="cols2"><div><h3 style="color:#8fc4e8">Meta <span class="pill">5</span></h3><p class="old" style="margin:-4px 0 10px">The builds most players run.</p><div class="stack"><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="priest-shadow-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Shadow</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Standard Shadow: hit from Shadow Focus, Improved Mind Blast, Mind Flay, Shadow Weaving, Darkness and Shadowform, with Discipline for Inner Focus and mana talents.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>18 / 0 / 33</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="priest-disc-healer.html"><span class="tag ">Healer</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Discipline healer</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Shields and crit heals: Renewed Hope and Divine Aegis turn crits into absorbs, Penance and Power Infusion at the bottom, Holy for crit chance and faster heals.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>31 / 20 / 0</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="priest-holy-healer.html"><span class="tag ">Healer</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Holy healer</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Raid healing through Spiritual Guidance, Spiritual Healing, Litany of Light and Prayer of Mending, with Discipline for mana (Mental Strength, Meditation, Mental Agility).</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>19 / 32 / 0</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="priest-shadow-leveling.html"><span class="tag lv">Leveling</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Shadow leveling</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Spirit Tap for downtime-free questing, Mind Flay at 20, Vampiric Embrace at 25 and Shadowform at 40, then Discipline for wand damage and mana.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>17 / 0 / 34</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="priest-disc-pvp.html"><span class="tag ">PvP</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Discipline/Shadow PvP</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Discipline to Power Infusion for shields and mana burn, plus Shadow's Blackout stuns, Improved Mind Blast and a shorter Psychic Scream.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>33 / 0 / 18</b> · level order →</p></a></div></div><div><h3 style="color:var(--ember)">Off-meta <span class="pill">1</span></h3><p class="old" style="margin:-4px 0 10px">Uncommon builds that can work – try something different.</p><div class="stack"><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="priest-smite.html"><span class="tag ">DPS</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Smite priest (Holy damage)</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Damage with Smite and Holy Fire: Power in Light, Holy Precision, Divine Fury, Searing Light and Spiritual Guidance, with a short Shadow dip for Shadow Word: Pain.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>19 / 25 / 7</b> · level order →</p></a></div></div></div><h2 id="shaman" style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px"><img src="../img/icons/class-shaman.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" style="border-radius:7px">Shaman</h2><div class="cols2"><div><h3 style="color:#8fc4e8">Meta <span class="pill">6</span></h3><p class="old" style="margin:-4px 0 10px">The builds most players run.</p><div class="stack"><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="shaman-ele-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Elemental</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Lightning Elemental: Call of Thunder crit, Lightning Overload, Elemental Fury and Lightning Mastery, with Restoration for mana and hit.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>32 / 5 / 14</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="shaman-enh-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Enhancement</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Stormstrike, Flurry, Maelstrom Weapon and Rage of the Farseer, with Elemental Devastation and Concussion for crit and lightning damage.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>8 / 33 / 10</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="shaman-resto-healer.html"><span class="tag ">Healer</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Restoration healer</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Deep Restoration for Riptide, Purification, Healing Way and Mana Tide Totem, with Thundering Strikes as the only off-tree pick.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>0 / 5 / 46</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="shaman-ele-leveling.html"><span class="tag lv">Leveling</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Elemental leveling</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Caster leveling with Elemental Focus, Trial by Fire and Earthbound for kiting, then Lightning Overload, Elemental Fury and Lightning Mastery; Restoration for mana.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>33 / 7 / 11</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="shaman-enh-leveling.html"><span class="tag lv">Leveling</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Enhancement leveling</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Melee leveling with Stormstrike, Improved Stormstrike, Spirit Weapons and early Flurry, plus Elemental crit (Elemental Devastation) and Trial by Fire.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>18 / 25 / 8</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="shaman-ele-pvp.html"><span class="tag ">PvP</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Elemental PvP</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Elemental burst to Lightning Mastery with Eye of the Storm and Elemental Warding, plus Enhancement Toughness, Guardian Totems, Earth's Grasp and Improved Ghost Wolf.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>31 / 20 / 0</b> · level order →</p></a></div></div><div><h3 style="color:var(--ember)">Off-meta <span class="pill">2</span></h3><p class="old" style="margin:-4px 0 10px">Uncommon builds that can work – try something different.</p><div class="stack"><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="shaman-elehance.html"><span class="tag ">DPS</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Elehance (Elemental/Enhancement)</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Splits points to get both Lightning Overload/Elemental Fury and Stormstrike/Flurry, weaving melee swings between Lightning Bolts.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>29 / 22 / 0</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="shaman-enh-tank.html"><span class="tag ">Tank</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Shaman tank (shield + Rockbiter)</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">One-hand + shield dungeon tank using Rockbiter threat, Spirit Weapons parry, Anticipation dodge and Improved Stormstrike resets, with Restoration for hit and mana.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>0 / 40 / 11</b> · level order →</p></a></div></div></div><h2 id="mage" style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px"><img src="../img/icons/class-mage.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" style="border-radius:7px">Mage</h2><div class="cols2"><div><h3 style="color:#8fc4e8">Meta <span class="pill">6</span></h3><p class="old" style="margin:-4px 0 10px">The builds most players run.</p><div class="stack"><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="mage-arcane-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Arcane Power</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Deep Arcane to Arcane Power and full Arcane Mind, dipping Fire for Ignite, Pyroblast and Heating Up plus Precision for hit.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>31 / 17 / 3</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="mage-fire-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Fire Combustion</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Full Fire to Combustion with Heating Up Pyroblasts, Critical Mass and Fire Power, topped up with Arcane Concentration and Missile Barrage.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>18 / 31 / 2</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="mage-frost-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Frost Fingers of Frost</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Frost to Ice Barrier with Fingers of Frost, Shatter and 5 Winter's Chill feeding Ice Lance and Cone of Cold, plus Arcane Concentration and Arcane Meditation.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>18 / 0 / 33</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="mage-frost-leveling.html"><span class="tag lv">Leveling</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Frost leveling</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Opens with 7 Arcane points for Missile Barrage, then goes deep Frost for Ice Lance, Fingers of Frost, Winter's Chill and Ice Barrier.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>13 / 5 / 33</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="mage-arcane-leveling.html"><span class="tag lv">Leveling</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Arcane leveling (chain-pull)</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Rushes Missile Barrage and Arcane Concentration, then fishes for procs with rank-1 Frostbolt to chain-pull with little drinking.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>32 / 16 / 3</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="mage-frost-pvp.html"><span class="tag ">PvP</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Frost PvP</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Frost with Frostbite, Permafrost, Improved Frost Nova and Shatter for root-and-burst, plus Improved Counterspell and Magic Absorption from Arcane.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>17 / 0 / 34</b> · level order →</p></a></div></div><div><h3 style="color:var(--ember)">Off-meta <span class="pill">1</span></h3><p class="old" style="margin:-4px 0 10px">Uncommon builds that can work – try something different.</p><div class="stack"><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="mage-frostfire.html"><span class="tag ">DPS</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Frostfire (Fire/Frost)</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">0/29/22 hybrid that casts Frostfire Bolt with Fire's Accelerant, Ignite and Heating Up, and Frost's Ice Shards, Shatter and Fingers of Frost.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>0 / 29 / 22</b> · level order →</p></a></div></div></div><h2 id="warlock" style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px"><img src="../img/icons/class-warlock.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" style="border-radius:7px">Warlock</h2><div class="cols2"><div><h3 style="color:#8fc4e8">Meta <span class="pill">9</span></h3><p class="old" style="margin:-4px 0 10px">The builds most players run.</p><div class="stack"><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="warlock-aff-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Affliction Demonic Sacrifice</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Deep Affliction with Wrack as filler, Pandemic, Soul Siphon and Shadow Mastery, plus Demonology for Demonic Sacrifice (Imp: +15% Shadow).</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>35 / 11 / 5</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="warlock-aff-ruin-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Affliction Ruin</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Wrack as filler with full Soul Siphon, plus 18 Destruction points for Improved Shadow Bolt, Bane, Ruin and Agonizing Flames.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>33 / 0 / 18</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="warlock-demo-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Demonology Demonic Pact</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">31 Demonology to Demonic Pact so you can sacrifice the Imp and keep the Sayaad, with Demonic Brand and Decimation, plus Improved Shadow Bolt/Bane/Ruin.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>2 / 31 / 18</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="warlock-destro-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Destruction Fire</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Petless Fire Destruction: sacrifice the Sayaad for +15% Fire, with Incinerate, Shadow and Flame, Fire and Brimstone, Ruin and Aftermath.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>7 / 11 / 33</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="warlock-destro-sayaad-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Destruction with Sayaad</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">The Sayaad stays out with Unholy Power 4, while Affliction gives hit, Improved Life Tap, Amplify Curse and Pandemic.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>14 / 4 / 33</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="warlock-aff-leveling.html"><span class="tag lv">Leveling</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Affliction leveling</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">No-respec Affliction leveling: instant Corruption and hit first, then Unholy Power for the pet, drain-tanking from 30 and Shadow Mastery late.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>40 / 7 / 4</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="warlock-drain-tank-leveling.html"><span class="tag lv">Leveling</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Drain-tank leveling (Voidwalker)</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Drain-tank leveling: the Voidwalker tanks while Wrack, Soul Siphon and Fel Concentration keep drains going, with Demonology for a tougher, cheaper pet.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>33 / 18 / 0</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="warlock-demo-leveling.html"><span class="tag lv">Leveling</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Demonology leveling</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Respec at 27 so the Sayaad holds 2-3 mobs with Demonic Brand, building to Demonic Pact at 40, then Affliction for instant Corruption and hit.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>20 / 31 / 0</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="warlock-destro-pvp.html"><span class="tag ">PvP</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Destruction PvP</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Bursty Fire Destruction for PvP, with Molten Skin damage reduction, Intensity against pushback, Pyroclasm stuns and Demonology for Stamina and Sayaad control.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>0 / 13 / 38</b> · level order →</p></a></div></div><div><h3 style="color:var(--ember)">Off-meta <span class="pill">0</span></h3><p class="old" style="margin:-4px 0 10px">Uncommon builds that can work – try something different.</p><div class="stack"><p class="old">None yet.</p></div></div></div><h2 id="druid" style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px"><img src="../img/icons/class-druid.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" style="border-radius:7px">Druid</h2><div class="cols2"><div><h3 style="color:#8fc4e8">Meta <span class="pill">6</span></h3><p class="old" style="margin:-4px 0 10px">The builds most players run.</p><div class="stack"><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="druid-balance-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Moonkin</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Full 41-point Balance to Moonkin Form with Eclipse, Vengeance, Improved Starfire and Moonfury, plus 10 Restoration points.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>41 / 0 / 10</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="druid-cat-raid.html"><span class="tag ">Raid</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Feral cat</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Cat DPS with Rend and Tear, Predatory Discipline, Shifting Power, Blood Frenzy and Leader of the Pack, Nature's Reach for hit and Heart of the Wild for Strength.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>9 / 32 / 10</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="druid-bear-tank.html"><span class="tag ">Tank</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Feral bear tank</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Bear tank that can still cat: Lacerate and Primal Bite for threat, Feral Charge interrupt, Thick Hide, and Leader of the Pack/Rend and Tear for cat swaps.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>9 / 37 / 5</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="druid-resto-healer.html"><span class="tag ">Healer</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Restoration healer</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">HoT-focused Restoration to Wild Growth with Bloom, Improved Regrowth, Swiftmend and Nature's Swiftness, plus Balance for Genesis and Nature's Splendor.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>13 / 0 / 38</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="druid-feral-leveling.html"><span class="tag lv">Leveling</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Feral leveling</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Cat leveling with bear swaps: Furor, Feral Charge, Leader of the Pack, Rend and Tear and Shifting Power, with Genesis/Nature's Reach and Heart of the Wild.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>9 / 37 / 5</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="druid-resto-pvp.html"><span class="tag ">PvP</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Restoration PvP</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">PvP Restoration with Feral dips for escapes and interrupts: Feral Swiftness, Brutal Impact, Furor and Feral Charge, plus Wild Growth and Bloom.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>0 / 11 / 40</b> · level order →</p></a></div></div><div><h3 style="color:var(--ember)">Off-meta <span class="pill">2</span></h3><p class="old" style="margin:-4px 0 10px">Uncommon builds that can work – try something different.</p><div class="stack"><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="druid-guardian-tank.html"><span class="tag ">Tank</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Pure bear (no Balance)</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">No-Balance bear build: Furor, Natural Reaction 5, Lacerate, Primal Bite and Feral Charge for threat and avoidance, with Heart of the Wild and Naturalist.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>0 / 41 / 10</b> · level order →</p></a><a class="card" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block" href="druid-balance-leveling.html"><span class="tag lv">Leveling</span><h3 style="margin:8px 0 4px;font:800 18px var(--f-display);color:var(--gold-soft)">Balance multi-DoT leveling</h3><p style="margin:0;color:#d8cfbf;font-size:15.5px">Multi-DoT Balance leveling: Improved Entangling Roots and Overgrowth root up to 3 mobs while Moonfire and Insect Swarm tick, ending in Moonkin Form.</p><p class="split" style="margin:8px 0 0">Split <b>43 / 0 / 8</b> · level order →</p></a></div></div></div></div></div>
